From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: avcodec/v4l2m2m_dec: keep the pending packet until the capture format is known

The capture format is only known once the driver has parsed the stream
headers; until then VIDIOC_G_FMT fails and v4l2_try_start() returns an
error. If the 16 output buffers fill up before that, ff_v4l2_context_
enqueue_packet() returns EAGAIN and v4l2_receive_frame() keeps the packet
for the next call, but the try_start failure that follows jumps to the
fail path, which unrefs it. Every packet arriving in that window is lost,
and the frames after it decode against missing references up to the next
keyframe: blocks of wrong picture in every moving area.

Seen on the SM-T550 (Venus, MSM8916) with Firefox and with the ffmpeg CLI:
framemd5 against the software decoder showed 4-37 frames missing around
frame 13-20 and every frame up to the next keyframe different, at 360p,
480p, 720p and 1080p, varying from run to run with the header parsing
time. GStreamer's v4l2h264dec on the same kernel was bit-exact (600/600).

Wait for the source change (poll POLLPRI, 100 ms steps, at most 2 s) and
retry the start while a packet is pending, instead of dropping it.
---
diff --git a/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c b/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c
--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/videodev2.h>
+#include <poll.h>
 #include <sys/ioctl.h>
 
 #include "libavutil/hwcontext.h"
@@ -170,6 +171,21 @@
 
     if (!s->draining) {
         ret = v4l2_try_start(avctx);
+        /*
+         * The capture format is only known once the driver has parsed the
+         * stream headers (VIDIOC_G_FMT fails until then). If the output
+         * queue filled up first, the packet refused above (EAGAIN) is still
+         * pending, and the fail path below would drop it: every frame lost
+         * there breaks the references up to the next keyframe. Wait for the
+         * source change event instead (up to 2 s), then retry.
+         */
+        for (int i = 0; ret && ret != AVERROR(ENOMEM) && s->buf_pkt.size &&
+                        !capture->streamon && i < 20; i++) {
+            struct pollfd pfd = { .fd = s->fd, .events = POLLPRI };
+            if (poll(&pfd, 1, 100) < 0)
+                break;
+            ret = v4l2_try_start(avctx);
+        }
         if (ret) {
             /* can't recover */
             if (ret != AVERROR(ENOMEM))
